Package: amber-fonts
Version: @VERSION@-1
Architecture: all
Maintainer: Hyperquader <hyperquader@gmail.com>
Installed-Size: @SIZE@
Depends: fontconfig
Section: fonts
Priority: optional
Homepage: https://github.com/Hyperquader-Coders/amber-fonts
Description: Source typeface family for the Amber Linux suite
 The typefaces every Amber Linux application draws with, packaged once so
 that copal, kat800 and amberlin depend on them instead of each carrying
 their own copy of the same files.
 .
 Five families are shipped and they are not interchangeable. "SauceCodePro
 Nerd Font" draws its icons at their natural width, which is what Copal and
 Amberlin want because they draw notes rather than a grid. "SauceCodePro
 Nerd Font Mono" squeezes each icon into exactly one character cell, which
 is what kat800 needs because VTE is a character grid. "Source Code Pro" is
 the same outlines without the icons, an order of magnitude smaller a face,
 for code that draws none. All three are monospaced. "Source Sans 3" and
 "Source Serif 4" are proportional and carry no icons either: they are
 Adobe's siblings of the same hand and skeleton, for prose that a monospaced
 face sets badly at any measure.
 .
 Every face is Adobe's, under the SIL Open Font License 1.1; the two
 SauceCodePro families are Adobe's code face with additional glyphs patched
 in by the Nerd Fonts project, renamed because the licence reserves the name
 "Source". No Debian package carries that patch, which is why the suite
 ships it itself: a missing family is a silent fallback to whatever Pango
 picks, which is invisible in the code and obvious on screen.
